cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FiVoHydro.jl — a finite-volume solver for boost-invariant relativistic viscous hydrodynamics with a diffusing heavy-quark charge"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ruwen
    family-names: Schulz
    email: ruwen-schulz@hotmail.de
repository-code: "https://github.com/RuwenSchulz/FiVoHydro.jl"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  FiVoHydro.jl (FiVo) solves boost-invariant relativistic viscous hydrodynamics in
  Milne coordinates together with a diffusing heavy-quark (charm) charge, in radial
  1+1D and transverse 2+1D. The scheme is conservative finite volume: HLLE with MUSCL
  reconstruction in primitive variables, SSPRK2/3 time stepping, operator-split
  relaxation of the dissipative fields, and a MOOD fallback. It ships a validation
  ladder in which every gate is judged by a referee that is not the code under test —
  a closed form, a semi-analytic ODE, or a second, independently written solver.
keywords:
  - relativistic hydrodynamics
  - heavy-ion collisions
  - heavy-quark diffusion
  - Israel-Stewart
  - finite volume
  - Julia
